## Why This Is Asked

This question tests practical debugging of a real-world programmable fabric where data-plane and control-plane interactions directly impact latency. Candidates must correlate low-level telemetry with high-level policy changes to isolate root causes and apply targeted mitigations.

## Key Concepts

- XDP/eBPF data-plane behavior under peak load
- ECMP/hash-based load balancing and collision dynamics
- SDN controller churn and policy stability requirements
- NIC offload pacing and interrupt coalescence interactions

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-diagnostic script outline
async function collectDiagnostics() {
  const [bpfStats, hashStats, sdnLogs, nicStats] = await Promise.all([
    getBpfMapStats(),
    getFlowHashDistribution(),
    getSdnPolicyChanges(),
    getNicOffloadMetrics()
  ]);

  return correlateLatencyWithMetrics(bpfStats, hashStats, sdnLogs, nicStats);
}
```
